&amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; &nbsp;

&#160; &#x00A0;

&unknownentity;

Prose carrying <!-- an inline comment --> and closing after it.

<!--
a comment
across lines
-->

&foo; &xy; &abcdefgh;

&a; &abcdefghij;

AN UNCLOSED COMMENT BUILDS NO COMMENT, and its own opening hyphens then read as a dash:

Prose carrying <!-- an opener with no closer on the line.

A comment holds markup as text, because nothing inside one parses: <!-- ''bold'' and [[a link]] -->
